  "golden_id": "tier0/semantics/export-padding-normal-combine",
  "tier": "0",
  "domain": "tier0/export/processing",
  "description": "Decision 293's Normal mesh-map combination probe (decision 276 item 5, phase1.25_pilot-wand item 2.7: how Painter combines a bound Normal mesh map with the padded mesh-free normal outside the islands), exploratory, under Legacy at 256 px, OpenGL. The authored mesh has two texture sets with the same UV layout, uzp_nc_mesh and uzp_nc_free, each four 48 x 48 texel islands centred in the quadrants of the tile, their borders on texel boundaries; the authored 16-bit Normal mesh map (per quadrant its own smooth field of normals tilted 10 to 45 degrees) is bound on uzp_nc_mesh only. On both sets: one fill with only Height active, the authored Height bitmap (flat, but a u v ramp on the two right-hand islands, constant on their top and left 24 texels), Normal at opacity 1; above it one fill with only Normal active, the authored Normal-channel bitmap (tilted 20 to 35 degrees), Normal at opacity 1, under a black mask whose fill effect is the authored mask (1 on the two bottom quadrants, 0 elsewhere). So uzp_nc_mesh holds the mesh map alone, with the Height ramp, with the channel patch and with both, and uzp_nc_free the same islands without the mesh map. Normal_OpenGL, Height and the Normal channel at OpenEXR 32f, and Normal_OpenGL at PNG 16, with infinite padding, no dithering, every export step done twice in the session.",
